==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Probably from Baltic *''sḗjlā'' (compare Lithuanian {{m|lt|siela}}), along with other Finnish loanwords from Baltic languages of the same thematic group, see etymology sections of e.g.{{m|fi|taivas||heaven}}, {{m|fi|Jumala||God}}. Another line of explanation links the word with a {{etyl|gem|fi}} language (compare Swedish {{m|sv|själ}}, German {{m|de|Seele}} and English {{m|en|soul}}).

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[soul]]
# [[moving spirit]] {{gloss|one who provides significant impetus or guidance in a given venture, movement, enterprise etc.}}

